00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:50,060
Language Takeaway.

139
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:51,400
Okay.

140
00:06:51,430 --> 00:06:56,410
So Jacob is talking to his mother and his mom wants to know, hey, how about these sneakers?

141
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:58,000
What do you think?

142
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,230
And Jacob says, Mom, they've got Velcro.

143
00:07:00,630 --> 00:07:00,910
Okay.

144
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:03,690
So Marco, what's this Velcro Jacob speaks of?

145
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:08,030
Well, as you can see, Velcro is capitalized, right?

146
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:11,840
And so that means this is a proper noun and it's actually a brand.

147
00:07:11,870 --> 00:07:12,190
Okay.

148
00:07:12,370 --> 00:07:13,350
It's like Chuck Taylors.

149
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:14,840
Like Chuck Taylors.

150
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:18,130
So Velcro is supposed kind of like a zipper, right?

151
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:19,360
A fastener.

152
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:23,390
But instead of zipping it up, you just put two pieces of cloth together and they stick.

153
00:07:23,950 --> 00:07:24,310
Okay.

154
00:07:24,430 --> 00:07:27,330
And when you pull them apart, they make that sound.

155
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:28,610
They make a loud sound.

156
00:07:29,130 --> 00:07:34,930
And so sometimes with baby shoes or young children's shoes, we don't want to tie them because that's too hard.

157
00:07:35,210 --> 00:07:36,170
So we have Velcro.

158
00:07:36,370 --> 00:07:39,170
This is a kind of fabric, like you said, that sticks together.

159
00:07:39,670 --> 00:07:43,030
We don't have to spend all this time tying things.

160
00:07:43,510 --> 00:07:49,250
So you see Velcro on hats, on gloves, on jackets, on shoes.

161
00:07:50,050 --> 00:07:55,780
It's a very popular way to make things, close things or to keep things secure.

162
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,340
In a very easy way, right?

163
00:07:57,440 --> 00:08:00,160
You just push them together and that's it.

164
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:00,560
They're sealed.

165
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,160
Exactly.

166
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:03,700
So the next time you see it, now you know that it's called Velcro.

167
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:07,520
I imagine in other languages, it's probably called the same thing.

168
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:08,520
Well, right.

169
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:08,940
It's the brand name.

170
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:10,520
Yeah.

171
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:11,520
Yeah.

172
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:12,520
So, okay.

173
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:16,150
And well, now moving on to the parts of the shoe, we have the tongue.

174
00:08:16,750 --> 00:08:17,090
Okay.

175
00:08:17,150 --> 00:08:19,270
Well, think about the body part, the tongue, right?

176
00:08:19,550 --> 00:08:23,890
When you look at your tongue, it's straight and it's flat and it kind of curves at the bottom.

177
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:25,640
Right.

178
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:29,640
So when you're putting your shoe on, you know, in the front of the shoe, you can make it stuck.

179
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:30,640
You have to pull the tongue.

180
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:31,640
Right.

181
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:36,360
It's a piece of fabric or piece of the shoe where the top of your foot is.

182
00:08:36,590 --> 00:08:36,970
Yeah.

183
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,360
Very good.

184
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:38,790
So that's called the tongue.

185
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:44,830
Now, some shoes have a very small tongue or a low one and others have a very high one.

186
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,560
Like for example, Chuck Taylors, they have a big tongue.

187
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,560
That's right.

188
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:49,560
Very long tongue.

189
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:52,670
And so the tongue is the part that rests on top of your foot.

190
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:55,870
And usually the shoelaces are over the tongue.

191
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:57,560
Exactly.

192
00:08:57,560 --> 00:09:01,650
And now moving on to the bottom part of the shoe, that's called the sole.

193
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:02,400
Okay.

194
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,080
S-O-L-E.

195
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:05,080
Sole.

196
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:06,320
This is a really important part of shoes.

197
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:14,280
I always look at the sole before I buy a pair of shoes because this is the part that you use the most because you're walking on the ground.

198
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:15,280
Right.

199
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:26,960
So for example, hiking boots, they will have a very high sole and they will have kind of like a pattern so that you don't slip if you're walking on dirt, right?

200
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:27,100
That's right.

201
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:30,320
Sometimes rubber, a rubber sole.

202
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:33,730
But other times, like Chuck Taylors also have a rubber sole but it's very thin.

203
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:34,530
It's very thin.

204
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:44,370
And some shoes, for example, they have a plastic sole maybe because they're used for other purposes so they might be a little bit slippery if you go onto a smooth surface.

205
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:45,880
Exactly.

206
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:48,010
So the sole, that's the bottom part of the shoe.

207
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:54,840
And the last part of the shoe that we're going to take a look at and probably the most important are the shoelaces.

208
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:56,440
Shoelaces.

209
00:09:56,440 --> 00:10:05,360
So shoelaces are basically long pieces of string that you use to tie your shoes closed because you want your shoes to be tight on your foot.

210
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:08,360
You don't want it to be too loose otherwise it might fall off.

211
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:16,950
And Chuck Taylors and some other shoes are very famous for having crazy colored laces or for people using crazy colored laces to tie them up.

212
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,320
Right.

213
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:20,950
So that's the part they use to tie or tighten the shoe with.

214
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:25,750
So on the opposite, if a shoe doesn't have shoelaces, it's probably going to have Velcro.

215
00:10:25,950 --> 00:10:26,270
That's right.

216
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,120
Velcro or shoelaces.

217
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,120
Okay.

218
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,950
So those are all the words that we have for you today.

219
